      "solution": ["use the marker's colour BEFORE a move: white means 1 place clockwise; grey or black means 2 places clockwise. Frames 1–6, marker position: lower-left → upper-left → top → right → bottom → lower-left. Next: upper-left.","from frame 3 the arrow points 135° clockwise from the marker TWO frames earlier. Frames 1–6, arrow direction: 180° clockwise from up → 270° clockwise from up → 0° clockwise from up → 90° clockwise from up → 135° clockwise from up → 225° clockwise from up. Next: 315° clockwise from up.","the marker colour cycles grey → white → black and repeats. Frames 1–6, marker colour: grey → white → black → grey → white → black. Next: grey.","the bottom dots cycle 2 → 1 → 4 → 3 and repeat. Frames 1–6, number of bottom dots: 2 → 1 → 4 → 3 → 2 → 1. Next: 4."],
